    "id": "a7821c42e6182e86e59e092e",
    "path": "datafusion_expr::udaf::SetMonotonicity",
    "name": "SetMonotonicity",
    "owner": null,
    "crate": "datafusion-expr",
    "version": "55.1.0",
    "kind": "enum",
    "signature": "enum SetMonotonicity",
    "docs": "Indicates whether an aggregation function is monotonic as a set\nfunction. A set function is monotonically increasing if its value\nincreases as its argument grows (as a set). Formally, `f` is a\nmonotonically increasing set function if `f(S) >= f(T)` whenever `S`\nis a superset of `T`.\n\nFor example `COUNT` and `MAX` are monotonically increasing as their\nvalues always increase (or stay the same) as new values are seen. On\nthe other hand, `MIN` is monotonically decreasing as its value always\ndecreases or stays the same as new values are seen.",
